`ls -l` marks a Btrfs subvolume made as a snapshot `[snapshot]`, or
`[snapshot, read-only]`, in place of the subvolume mark of patch 0011
(ADR 0461): a subvolume whose parent UUID is set, which Linux's
`BTRFS_IOC_GET_SUBVOL_INFO` tells anyone who can open the folder, and
Radix's C library asks the directory's `subvolume` method for. It is
asked only of folders that are the top of a subvolume.

